{"authored" [{"question" "q-36300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x,y)=2xy+{e}^{3x-y}.$ What is the magnitude of the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,3)$ in the direction in which the function decreases most rapidly?" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-36300/review.json" "file_sha256" "1e96dff6441a58c4c4e7eaabe4f2b3295e16b29c6f5517d3b2d0c0692aa412ae" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-36300/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "2b305b56a43af507a591835f0266e265c32e91511d4c5d8b2e906d4694388870" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-36300/verification.json" "basis" 2396 "rationale" "For f=2xy+exp(3x−y), grad=(2y+3exp(3x−y),2x−exp(3x−y)); at(1,3) grad=(9,1). Negative unit gradient gives signedrate−sqrt82, magnitude sqrt82. Source accepted positive sqrt82, so minimally clarify requested magnitude, prefix the retained original source calculation, and append the signed-rate note. All five original choices/answer/field IDs and source key remain unchanged; source artifacts, full original solution and historical version remain retained. Label only the final norm calculation as magnitude; the source negative-gradient algebra is already correct."} {"question" "q-36300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Interpret the positive quantity calculated below as the magnitude of the rate of change in the direction of fastest decrease.\n\nAt a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ decreases most rapidly in the opposite direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nIn our case, we compute $-∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-∇\\,f(x,y) & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy+{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }i-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-(2y+3{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }i-(2x-{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }j \\\\ -∇\\,f(1,3) & =-(2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot {e}^{3\\cdot 1-3})\\text{ }i-(2\\cdot 1-{e}^{3\\cdot 1-3})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-9\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the magnitude of the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,3)$ in the direction of $-∇f(1,3)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-∇\\,f(1,3)‖ & =‖-9\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{82}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSigned-rate note: $\\nabla f(1,3)=(9,1)$ and the unit direction of fastest decrease is $\\mathbf u=(-9,-1)/\\sqrt{82}$. Therefore $D_{\\mathbf u}f(1,3)=\\nabla f(1,3)\\cdot\\mathbf u=-\\sqrt{82}$. Its magnitude is $\\sqrt{82}$, which is the positive quantity requested in the clarified study question." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-36300/review.json" "file_sha256" "1e96dff6441a58c4c4e7eaabe4f2b3295e16b29c6f5517d3b2d0c0692aa412ae" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-36300/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "2b305b56a43af507a591835f0266e265c32e91511d4c5d8b2e906d4694388870" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-36300/verification.json" "basis" 2396 "rationale" "For f=2xy+exp(3x−y), grad=(2y+3exp(3x−y),2x−exp(3x−y)); at(1,3) grad=(9,1). Negative unit gradient gives signedrate−sqrt82, magnitude sqrt82. Source accepted positive sqrt82, so minimally clarify requested magnitude, prefix the retained original source calculation, and append the signed-rate note. All five original choices/answer/field IDs and source key remain unchanged; source artifacts, full original solution and historical version remain retained. Label only the final norm calculation as magnitude; the source negative-gradient algebra is already correct."} {"question" "q-36300" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{82}"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-36300/review.json" "file_sha256" "1e96dff6441a58c4c4e7eaabe4f2b3295e16b29c6f5517d3b2d0c0692aa412ae" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-36300/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "2b305b56a43af507a591835f0266e265c32e91511d4c5d8b2e906d4694388870" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-36300/verification.json" "basis" 2396 "rationale" "For f=2xy+exp(3x−y), grad=(2y+3exp(3x−y),2x−exp(3x−y)); at(1,3) grad=(9,1). Negative unit gradient gives signedrate−sqrt82, magnitude sqrt82. Source accepted positive sqrt82, so minimally clarify requested magnitude, prefix the retained original source calculation, and append the signed-rate note. All five original choices/answer/field IDs and source key remain unchanged; source artifacts, full original solution and historical version remain retained. Label only the final norm calculation as magnitude; the source negative-gradient algebra is already correct."} {"question" "q-36300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x,y)=2xy+{e}^{3x-y}.$ What is the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,3)$ in the direction in which the function decreases most rapidly?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ decreases most rapidly in the opposite direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nIn our case, we compute $-∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-∇\\,f(x,y) & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy+{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }i-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-(2y+3{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }i-(2x-{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }j \\\\ -∇\\,f(1,3) & =-(2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot {e}^{3\\cdot 1-3})\\text{ }i-(2\\cdot 1-{e}^{3\\cdot 1-3})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-9\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,3)$ in the direction of $-∇f(1,3)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-∇\\,f(1,3)‖ & =‖-9\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{82}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c362cd907fb85830ab3320317ae756b56808309a5fb6a6d98274061b8fc74a3f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36300" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json" "file_sha256" "abc84f7aef8805102238c63265050a108257d205b44bbf08f3fcd9e3a1c4529f" "basis" 2394 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_